.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH ferroclass-ansible 1  "ferroclass-ansible 0.11.1" 
.SH NAME
ferroclass\-ansible \- Ansible dynamic inventory adapter for reclass
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBferroclass\-ansible\fR [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-applications\-postfix\fR] [\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-storage\-type\fR] [\fB\-b\fR|\fB\-\-inventory\-base\-uri\fR] [\fB\-u\fR|\fB\-\-nodes\-uri\fR] [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-classes\-uri\fR] [\fB\-\-parameter\-key\-style\fR] [\fB\-a\fR|\fB\-\-compose\-node\-name\fR] [\fB\-z\fR|\fB\-\-ignore\-class\-notfound\fR] [\fB\-x\fR|\fB\-\-ignore\-class\-notfound\-regexp\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-pretty\-print\fR] [\fB\-\-output\-sorted\fR] [\fB\-0\fR|\fB\-\-multiple\-errors\fR] [\fB\-1\fR|\fB\-\-single\-error\fR] [\fB\-l\fR|\fB\-\-list\fR] [\fB\-t\fR|\fB\-\-host\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Ansible dynamic inventory adapter for reclass
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
enable verbose logging
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH "ANSIBLE OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-applications\-postfix\fR \fI<APPLICATIONS_POSTFIX>\fR [default: _hosts]
postfix to append to applications to turn them into groups
.SH "DATABASE OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-storage\-type\fR \fI<STORAGE_TYPE>\fR
the type of storage backend to use
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
yaml\-fs: YAML file system storage (directory\-based)
.IP \(bu 2
yaml\-file: YAML file storage (single file with multiple documents)
.RE
.TP
\fB\-b\fR, \fB\-\-inventory\-base\-uri\fR \fI<INVENTORY_BASE_URI>\fR
the base URI to prepend to nodes and classes
.TP
\fB\-u\fR, \fB\-\-nodes\-uri\fR \fI<NODES_URI>\fR
the URI to the node storage
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-classes\-uri\fR \fI<CLASSES_URI>\fR
the URI to the class storage
.TP
\fB\-\-parameter\-key\-style\fR \fI<PARAMETER_KEY_STYLE>\fR
parameter key validation style
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
none: No validation of parameter keys
.IP \(bu 2
ansible: Ansible variable name rules (letters, numbers, underscores only)
.RE
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-compose\-node\-name\fR
compose node names from subdirectory paths
.TP
\fB\-z\fR, \fB\-\-ignore\-class\-notfound\fR
ignore classes that are not found instead of raising an error
.TP
\fB\-x\fR, \fB\-\-ignore\-class\-notfound\-regexp\fR \fI<PATTERN>\fR
regexp pattern for class names to ignore when not found (can be specified multiple times)
.SH "OUTPUT OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR [default: json]
output format (default: json)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
yaml: YAML output format
.IP \(bu 2
json: JSON output format
.RE
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-pretty\-print\fR
pretty\-print output (indented, newlines)
.TP
\fB\-\-output\-sorted\fR
sort keys alphabetically in output
.TP
\fB\-0\fR, \fB\-\-multiple\-errors\fR
group multiple resolve errors and report them together instead of failing on the first error
.TP
\fB\-1\fR, \fB\-\-single\-error\fR
report only the first resolve error instead of grouping all errors
.SH MODES
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-list\fR
output the entire inventory
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-host\fR \fI<HOSTNAME>\fR
output host variables for a specific host
.SH EXTRA
This binary implements the Ansible dynamic inventory protocol.
Use \-\-list to output the entire inventory as JSON.
Use \-\-host HOSTNAME to output host variables for a specific node.
.SH VERSION
v0.11.1
